# Laziness proof: $map callback not called when the mapped result is never accessed.
# The mapped dict is stored in "expensive", which is never accessed.
# If map were eager, the [raise "should not fire"] callback would execute and error.
# Since dict entries are lazy thunks and "expensive" is unused, the callback is
# never invoked and no error fires.
[cheap: 7
 expensive: [map [fn [x] [raise "should not fire"]] [p: 1  q: 2  r: 3]]]
---
%.cheap
=== out
Int(7)
